<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices-April 28.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices-April 28.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for April 28.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Apr    218.00    221.50    222.00     229.00</p>
<p>    May    218.00    221.50    222.00     229.00</p>
<p>    Jun    211.00    214.50    215.00     227.50</p>
<p>    Jul    207.00    210.50    211.00     225.00</p>
<p>    Aug    206.00    209.50    210.00     224.00</p>
<p>    Sept   206.00    209.50    210.00     224.00</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased A$1.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	198.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  173.50	    Port Adelaide	 175.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     173.75	    Port Giles	    175.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	171.50	    Wallaroo		173.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    170.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     173.50	    Port Lincoln	  176.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   174.00	    Thevenard	     171.75</p>
<p>Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 173.00	     Esperance	    178.25</p>
<p>    Portland	174.00	     Albany		 179.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    181.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    179.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Time (0630 GMT).  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
